  "comment": [
    "Aisle-classifier accuracy fixture. 80 items written the way a person actually",
    "types them into a shopping list, with the aisle a shopper would expect.",
    "",
    "WRITTEN BEFORE MEASURING, and deliberately NOT derived from src/aisles.js - the",
    "point is to find what the keyword table misses, and a fixture read off the table",
    "can only ever score 100%. It replaces the old 26-item brand set, which could not",
    "separate differences smaller than ~8 points (see DONE.md 2026-07-26).",
    "",
    "GENUINELY AMBIGUOUS ITEMS ARE EXCLUDED, not guessed at. 'seltzer' (Beverages or",
    "Alcohol), 'marshmallows' (Snacks or Baking), 'apple sauce' (Pantry or Produce)",
    "and 'lemon juice' (bottled is Pantry, squeezed is Produce) have no single right",
    "answer, so scoring them would measure our opinion rather than the classifier.",
    "",
    "Items marked \"held\": true are a HOLD-OUT set - do not add keywords for these",
    "in response to a miss. They exist to show whether a fix generalised or was just",
    "taught to the test. Score them separately from the rest."
  ],
